ui/gtk: quick boot, saved states, pause, gestures, pasted text

For the ASoftware side bar (0006-0008):
- quick-boot=on: closing the window saves the machine as the internal
  snapshot "asoft-quick" (a Saving cover meanwhile) and quits. Started
  with -loadvm asoft-quick it resumes and deletes that snapshot once it
  runs, so a state is never resumed twice. A failed save shuts the guest
  down instead. (A migration to a file would keep the window drawing,
  but QEMU's file: migration does not work on Windows.)
- STATE: Pause/Resume (a Paused cover; a click on it goes on), Save state
  (internal snapshot "state-<time>", with a Saving cover), Saved states...
  (restore or delete one).
- App switcher: a touch gesture up from the bottom edge, held still.
- The mouse wheel swipes where the pointer is: iOS has no wheel.
- Paste text (Ctrl+V): the PC clipboard typed on the guest keyboard, a
  US layout, printable ASCII; Ctrl+S screenshot, F11 full screen.
Based on QEMU v11.1.2 with 0002-0008.

